---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

// Change this date whenever the policy text changes.
const updated = { iso: '2026-11-25', label: '25 November 2026' };

const sections = [
  ['introduction', 'Introduction'],
  ['information-we-collect', 'Information we collect'],
  ['personal-information', 'Personal information'],
  ['automatically-collected', 'Automatically collected information'],
  ['how-we-use', 'How information is used'],
  ['storage-security', 'Data storage and security'],
  ['cookies', 'Cookies and tracking technologies'],
  ['third-parties', 'Third-party services'],
  ['sharing', 'Data sharing'],
  ['retention', 'Data retention'],
  ['your-rights', 'Your privacy rights'],
  ['children', 'Children’s privacy'],
  ['transfers', 'International data transfers'],
  ['changes', 'Changes to this policy'],
];
const num = (id: string) => sections.findIndex(([s]) => s === id) + 1;
const title = (id: string) => `${num(id)}. ${sections[num(id) - 1][1]}`;
---
<MainLayout title="Privacy Policy | Litenly" description="How Litenly handles your photos, documents and app data on your iPhone, and what this website collects.">
  <PageHeader title="Privacy Policy">
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime={updated.iso}>{updated.label}</time></p>
  </PageHeader>

  <div class="section">
    <Container narrow>
      <nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-title">
        <h2 id="toc-title">Contents</h2>
        <ol>{sections.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}</ol>
      </nav>

      <article>
        <h2 id="introduction">{title('introduction')}</h2>
        <p>This policy covers the {site.fullName} app for iPhone (bundle identifier <code>{site.bundleId}</code>) and this website. In this policy, “we” and “us” mean the publisher of the app.</p>
        <p>In short: the app processes your files on your iPhone. It has no user accounts, advertising, analytics tools or crash-reporting tools from third parties, and it does not upload your photos or documents to us.</p>

        <h2 id="information-we-collect">{title('information-we-collect')}</h2>
        <p>The app does not send information to us. To do its job, it accesses and stores the following <strong>on your device</strong>:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Files you choose:</strong> photos, image files and PDF documents that you open for compression.</li>
          <li><strong>Photo library:</strong> if you use Smart Gallery, the app reads the photos you choose, or your library if you scan it, and writes new copies or replacements when you confirm. Saving a result to Photos requires permission to add photos.</li>
          <li><strong>Image metadata:</strong> details embedded in a file, such as format, dimensions, date and location. Single-image compression removes metadata and location by default; you can choose to keep supported metadata. A file already within your limits may be used as it is. Compress in Place keeps date and time, location, favourite status, regular albums and hidden status where iOS allows.</li>
          <li><strong>Compression history:</strong> file names, sizes, dimensions, dates, where a result was saved, copies of compressed outputs and small preview thumbnails.</li>
          <li><strong>Smart Gallery records:</strong> photo identifiers, file sizes and a record of the jobs, copies and replacements, so the app can verify results and avoid repeating work.</li>
          <li><strong>Preferences and temporary files:</strong> settings such as appearance, remembered photo choices, reminder and alert settings, and working files created during compression.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="personal-information">{title('personal-information')}</h2>
        <p>The app does not ask for your name, email address, phone number, payment details or an account, and we do not collect them through it. Your files may contain personal information, but it is processed on your device.</p>

        <h2 id="automatically-collected">{title('automatically-collected')}</h2>
        <p><strong>App:</strong> we do not include code that automatically sends usage, device or diagnostic information to us. Apple may collect information about App Store downloads, and may share diagnostics with developers if you have allowed this in iOS. Apple’s own privacy policy applies.</p>
        <p><strong>Website:</strong> this website contains no analytics scripts or contact forms. The company hosting it may record standard server logs, such as IP address, browser type, requested page and time.</p>

        <h2 id="how-we-use">{title('how-we-use')}</h2>
        <p>Information on your device is used only to provide app features:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>compressing, resizing, converting and previewing your files;</li>
          <li>estimating possible savings and verifying copies and replacements;</li>
          <li>showing history and your settings;</li>
          <li>sending the local reminders and low-storage alerts you turn on.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="storage-security">{title('storage-security')}</h2>
        <p>App data is stored in the app’s private storage on your iPhone and relies on the protections of iOS and your device passcode. Depending on your iOS settings, some app data may be included in device backups, such as iCloud Backup. No method of storage is completely secure.</p>
        <p>Smart Gallery does not download photos that exist only in iCloud. When you pick a photo with the iOS photo picker, iOS may download it from iCloud so it can be provided to the app.</p>
        <h3>Permissions</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Photos:</strong> to read the photos used by Smart Gallery and to save results. You can grant limited access, or change access at any time in iOS Settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> only for reminders and low-storage alerts. These are created on your device.</li>
          <li><strong>Background refresh:</strong> to check free storage for the optional low-storage alert.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="cookies">{title('cookies')}</h2>
        <p>This website does not set cookies and uses no tracking technologies. Fonts and images are served with the site. The app does not use tracking technologies or track you across other apps and websites.</p>

        <h2 id="third-parties">{title('third-parties')}</h2>
        <p>The app includes no third-party software libraries or services. It uses features provided by Apple, such as Photos, Files, notifications and the share sheet. Links that open in your browser lead to pages with their own privacy practices.</p>

        <h2 id="sharing">{title('sharing')}</h2>
        <p>Because the app does not send your files or app data to us, we do not sell or share them. When you save or share a result, you choose the destination, and that app or service handles it under its own policy.</p>

        <h2 id="retention">{title('retention')}</h2>
        <p>App data stays on your device until you remove it:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>delete individual history entries or clear your history;</li>
          <li>use <strong>Settings, then Clear All Data</strong> to remove history, scan results, settings, reminders and temporary files;</li>
          <li>delete the app to remove its private storage. Existing device backups follow your backup settings.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These actions do not delete photos or files you saved to Photos, Files or elsewhere. Originals you move to Recently Deleted are managed by Apple Photos. Any server logs recorded by the website host are retained according to that provider’s practices.</p>

        <h2 id="your-rights">{title('your-rights')}</h2>
        <p>You control the data in the app: you can change permissions, delete history, clear all data or delete the app. Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or restrict the processing of personal data, to object to processing, and to complain to a data protection authority.</p>

        <h2 id="children">{title('children')}</h2>
        <p>The app has no accounts and does not send personal information to us.</p>

        <h2 id="transfers">{title('transfers')}</h2>
        <p>The app does not transfer your files or app data to us in any country. Any server logs recorded by the website host may be processed in the countries where that provider operates.</p>

        <h2 id="changes">{title('changes')}</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy, for example when app features change. The updated version will be posted on this page with a new “Last updated” date.</p>
      </article>
    </Container>
  </div>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .toc { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.5rem; }
  .toc h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .toc ol { columns: 2; column-gap: 2rem; margin: 0; padding-left: 1.35rem; }
  .toc li { break-inside: avoid; }
  .toc a { display: inline-block; padding: 0.3rem 0; text-decoration: none; }
  .toc a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  article h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 0.25rem; }
  article h3 { margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  li { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }
  code { font-size: 0.9em; background: var(--green-tint); padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 5px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .toc ol { columns: 1; } }
</style>
